From 62c34a48c6588ba9bb18722010383d03b481f778 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olivier Louvignes <olivier@mgcrea.io>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:00:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 60/61] mmc: jz4740: remove the host before resetting the
 controller

Removing the driver masked every interrupt and reset the controller
before mmc_remove_host(), which removes the card and lets its driver
send its last commands. Those commands still go out, but the first one
after the reset can wait for the driver's 5 s request timeout.

With an SDIO card that cost 5 s on every unbind: on the HiBy R1 (X1600,
a BCM43430A1 on brcmfmac), the CMD52 with which sdio_release_irq()
reads the card's interrupt enables, in brcmfmac's remove, waited 5 s
while MSC_STAT showed the command finished (END_CMD_RES) and MSC_IMASK
read 0xffffffff, although the request had unmasked END_CMD_RES. On the
X1600, MSC_STAT can still show IS_RESETTING after jz4740_mmc_reset()
returns, so the reset most likely finished after that write and undid
it.

Remove the host first, then quiesce the controller.
---
 drivers/mmc/host/jz4740_mmc.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/jz4740_mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/jz4740_mmc.c
index e845a6f..333a6b8 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/jz4740_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/jz4740_mmc.c
@@ -1325,12 +1325,13 @@ static void jz4740_mmc_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct jz4740_mmc_host *host = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
+	/* The card's driver may still send commands as it goes */
+	mmc_remove_host(host->mmc);
+
 	timer_delete_sync(&host->timeout_timer);
 	jz4740_mmc_set_irq_enabled(host, 0xff, false);
 	jz4740_mmc_reset(host);
 
-	mmc_remove_host(host->mmc);
-
 	free_irq(host->irq, host);
 
 	if (host->use_dma)
-- 
